diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 4479b53..e7703d5 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -9,6 +9,45 @@ pnpm install && pnpm run start
 
 The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 
+## Phone verification during sign-up
+
+Sign-up collects an international phone number, sends an SMS, checks the six-digit
+code on the server, and then submits the account to the existing registration
+service. Passwords are kept in component memory until registration and are never
+stored in the verification session. Codes and credentials are not logged.
+
+Configure the server environment using the variables in [.env.example](.env.example).
+Use a Twilio Verify Service with a **six-digit code length** and an approved
+[domain-bound SMS template](https://www.twilio.com/en-us/blog/developers/tutorials/product/domain-bound-sms-otps-verify).
+Set `TWILIO_VERIFY_TEMPLATE_SID` to that template's SID. Its last line must contain
+the actual sign-up host (no scheme, path, or port), a single space, and the code:
+
+```text
+Your DevTools Times verification code is 012345.
+
+@your-domain.example #012345
+```
+
+Twilio supplies the generated code through the template's code variable. Configure
+the template for the deployed host, and serve the site over HTTPS. WebOTP listens
+before SMS delivery and automatically submits a received code when supported;
+other browsers retain keyboard autofill, paste, and manual entry. Resends are
+limited to every 30 seconds per session; codes expire within 10 minutes and allow
+five checks per challenge. Also configure Twilio Verify fraud protection and
+provider rate limits for the deployment. Missing credentials disable SMS delivery
+with an explanatory form error; there is no simulated success or test-code bypass.
+
+The Node adapter stores verification state in server-side sessions. Deployments
+with multiple instances need a shared session driver. Runtime credentials must be
+exported by the host; the production Node entrypoint does not load `.env` files.
+This app gates its own registration endpoint on verification and forwards the
+verified phone number to the existing external registration API. The externally
+hosted API is unchanged; enforcing verification for all callers and persisting the
+phone on the account also requires support in that service.
+
+Run `pnpm test` (Node 22.18+ or 24+) for mocked SMS and registration tests, and
+`pnpm build` for the production build. These checks do not send SMS.
+
 ## Tech Stack
 
 - **[Astro](https://astro.build/)**: The web framework for building content-driven websites.
